  "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a man in a formal setting, likely a congressional hearing, with the text overlay \"state your name for the record\" and \"what page is it on?\". The juxtaposition humorously implies that the man is so accustomed to bureaucratic or procedural formalities that he is confused about basic record-keeping, suggesting he is either overly bureaucratic or out of touch with simple administrative tasks. The meme is not targeting any specific group based on protected characteristics, nor does it contain abusive, cyberbullying, hateful, misogynistic, or propagandistic content. However, it is potentially harmful because it could be used to mock individuals in positions of authority or to undermine their competence in a public forum, which may contribute to a culture of disrespect or cynicism toward institutional processes. The intent is satirical, using the visual of a serious official to contrast with the absurdity of the question, thereby highlighting perceived incompetence or absurdity in bureaucratic systems.",
